# Welcome to Markdown Viewer 3.10.3

_Released September 28, 2026_

This release adds a responsive Document Outline and configurable Copy TOC workflow, gives every public language page useful translated content from the first response, and improves Markdown typography and RTL list rendering.

Everything here ships with the web, PWA, Docker, and desktop editions. **Happy coding!**

[View release on GitHub](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/releases/tag/v3.10.3) [Open the full changelog](https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)

---

## Highlights

- **See the shape of a long document.** Open a live H1–H6 tree, fold heading branches, track the current section, and jump without leaving Editor, Preview, or Split mode.
- **Copy a TOC that matches the Preview.** Choose heading depth and output style, normalize skipped levels when useful, or wrap linked output in a collapsible section.
- **Start every language page in its language.** All 15 public URLs now serve translated visible content and starter documents before JavaScript runs, with matching metadata and canonical identity.
- **Keep document typography independent from the interface.** Japanese and Korean UI choices no longer restyle Markdown or release notes.
- **Render RTL lists like readers expect.** Right-to-left bullets stay inside the content area, and list-to-paragraph spacing follows GitHub-style Markdown presentation.

> [!TIP]
> Open **Document Outline** with the book-text button after Full Screen. Choose **Copy table of contents** for the default H2–H4 linked list, or open its settings for H1–H6 limits, numbered links, plain text, normalization, and a collapsible wrapper.

## Navigate with Document Outline

Document Outline adds a responsive right sidebar built around the current document's H1–H6 structure. Parent headings have collapsible branches and subtle hierarchy guides, while **Collapse/Expand All** controls the full tree. The active section follows scrolling, and selecting a heading jumps to the right source or rendered position without changing Editor, Preview, or Split mode.

The outline updates as you edit, import, or switch documents. Code-block headings are excluded, read-only documents remain navigable, and collapsed branches retain their state while content changes. On small screens the panel leaves room for the document and closes after navigation.

Document Outline and Find & Replace now use matching text-only headers, a 340px default width, and the same resize behavior as Explorer. Drag the edge, use arrow keys for precise sizing, hold Shift for larger steps, or use Home or a double-click to restore the default.

## Copy a dependable Markdown TOC

**Copy table of contents** works directly from the current Markdown AST, so it does not wait for Preview, modify the document, or omit headings hidden inside collapsed outline branches. The default includes H2–H4 as nested bulleted links. Settings support any H1–H6 range, hierarchical numbered links, plain indented text, skipped-level normalization, and an optional `<details>` wrapper for linked output.

Copied links and Preview headings share the same GitHub-compatible anchors. Unicode letters and underscores remain, punctuation and emoji are removed consistently, duplicate headings receive stable `-1`, `-2`, and later suffixes, and symbol-only headings receive a documented fallback. YAML front matter and fenced code are excluded, while inline formatting is reduced to its visible heading text.

## Useful localized content from the first response

Previously, localized URLs could provide translated metadata and interface labels while their initial visible body and first-run document remained English. The root English URL and all 14 translated `?lang=` URLs now serve language-matched welcome content directly in the initial HTML, plus an appropriate starter document for new visitors.

The public URL is now authoritative: `/` remains English and a supported `?lang=` selects that language without a saved or browser preference silently overriding it. Titles, canonicals, schema, response language, visible content, and the client stay aligned, while changing the interface never translates or replaces an existing document.

Development now exercises the same SEO middleware used by Cloudflare Pages. A new read-only `npm run audit:seo` command checks deployed canonical responses, language alternates, redirects, and discovery files; it verifies technical delivery without claiming or changing Google indexing status.

## Consistent multilingual Markdown rendering

Selecting Japanese or Korean no longer applies interface-language spacing, line-height, justification, wrapping, or heading-weight changes to user-authored Markdown or release notes. Documents now retain the same typography as you switch interface languages, including mixed-language text, frontmatter, headings, and tables.

RTL list rendering now uses right-side padding with left padding removed at the required specificity, keeping bullets and task-list controls inside the content boundary. Standard lists also inherit GitHub-style spacing before following paragraphs instead of the previous compressed custom margins.

## Quality, offline use, and desktop parity

The pure TOC generator has dedicated Node unit coverage and produces a committed browser/worker bundle with dependency license notices. Static validation checks the source, generated bundle, required page IDs, and desktop parity. The PWA caches the TOC bundle and localized welcome module, and the Neutralino resources include the same outline, copy, locale, typography, and RTL behavior as the web app.

